comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T21:34:36.710Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-07-31: release automation now installs the exact registry version into unrelated npm and Bun roots, asserts executable containment, and runs a ten-step cold agent lifecycle covering init, orient, create, claim, annotate, evidence linking, close, validate, and context with per-step output bounds and aggregate token cost. Failure reports name the manager and step; unit controls cover containment and budget failures. Live 2026.7.31 acceptance passed for both managers: 10 steps each, 19,568 characters and 4,892 estimated tokens. This item remains active because the hosted OS matrix and previous-release control session are not yet implemented."
  "2026-07-31T21:51:09.098Z","harness:codex","CI portability evidence 2026-07-31: Windows exposed that the installed-agent escape negative control recognized only POSIX node_modules/.bin separators. The fixture now uses node:path separators and derives an outside path on the current drive, preserving the same containment assertion on Windows and POSIX. The focused 8-test verifier suite passes, ESLint passes, and the full 6,623-test coverage run remains exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-31T22:25:41.756Z","harness:codex","Review-loop release evidence 2026-07-31: registry installs now retry transient failures three times with bounded production backoff, Bun disables lifecycle scripts, synchronous subprocesses enforce timeout/input invariants, pm-mcp initialize has a 60-second deadline, and missing executable coverage fails before any registry execution. Negative controls and exact cross-platform tests pass; the complete 6,625-test suite is 100/100/100/100 and quality:static is green. Hosted OS-matrix and previous-release control acceptance remain open."
  "2026-08-03T11:17:40.251Z","harness:codex","Partial acceptance evidence 2026-08-03: scripts/release/verify-published-release.mjs passed against exact version 2026.8.3 for registry integrity, npx and bunx real command dispatch, both executor MCP handshakes, bin coverage, missing-command negative controls, and GitHub Release metadata. The item remains open because its broader clean-install scripted agent-session and advertisement-order contract was not re-proved by this command alone."
  "2026-08-09T16:21:34.768Z","harness:codex","Published 2026.8.9 acceptance evidence: both npm and Bun clean installs completed init, orient, create, claim, annotate, link evidence, close, validate, read-back, and context-read-back within their output ceilings. The report returned ok:true for both managers, but final temp-root removal raised ENOTEMPTY and made the wrapper exit 1; cleanup ownership is canonical pm-p5u6, so this item remains open for its existing OS-matrix and previous-release residuals."
  "2026-08-15T01:33:29.338Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-15: the local packed-artifact release gate hung for more than 11 minutes inside npm exec despite a valid tarball. Local-tarball npx/npm execution is now explicitly offline and every subprocess has a 120-second timeout. The 24-test smoke suite passes, including a new negative-control contract that every relevant subprocess is offline and all subprocesses are bounded; the real packed smoke completes in about 15 seconds with version 2026.8.14 and 13 packages. The broader hosted OS-matrix and previous-release residuals remain open on this canonical item."
  "2026-08-15T02:58:00.044Z","harness:codex","PR #1016 CI correction 2026-08-15: --offline was valid only on a warmed local npm cache and failed a clean GitHub runner with ENOTCACHED for @sentry/node. Local-tarball npm/npx installs now allow dependency resolution while every subprocess retains the 120-second deadline. The 24-test smoke suite, real packed tarball smoke (2026.8.14, 13 packages), typecheck, and exact 7,337-test 100/100/100/100 coverage pass. Hosted OS-matrix and previous-release residuals remain open."
  "2026-08-15T03:01:46.864Z","harness:codex","Pause evidence: the PR smoke correction and linked acceptance tests are complete (64/64 across two links), but the broader released-artifact OS matrix and previous-release acceptance residuals remain open for future active work."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T10:48:39.250Z","harness:claude-code","Measured 2026-07-26 against the published 2026.7.26: post-publish verification covers execution only. verify-published-release.mjs runs npx --yes <pkg> --version, npx --yes --package <pkg> -- pm --version, and bunx --bun <pkg> pm --version. No install path is exercised for any manager — not npm install -g, not a project install, not bun add, not pnpm add — so packaging omissions and binary-link defects reach users through a green pipeline. Confirmed working by hand and therefore available as a starting fixture: bun add @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.26 links pm, pm-cli, and pm-mcp, and pm init, pm create, and pm list all succeed under the Bun runtime. The third check's invocation shape is separately defective and is owned by pm-lpqln4."
